      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CARDIGAN DAN (8) has been freshened since fading out of a Victoria Derby heat last time but is much better than that having finished runner-up in the Vicbred final prior. Draws for a trail and is two for two at this distance. He looks well placed. WHERE IS WOODY (2) has been competitive of late and kept the ball rolling when 1.4 metres from the winner in second here last week. Should have no excuses from another good draw. DECODE (3) didn't do a bad job in a handy line-up last time out. Won two of his previous three and is suited dropping to a distance where he is unbeaten. EL LAZZAR (6) must be included after winning three of his past four starts including his lone attempt at this circuit and distance. HANDLER (1) is improving with racing this time in and draws to advantage.",
